01:05:37,684 --> 01:05:38,977
Please answer.

282
01:06:16,347 --> 01:06:18,433
<i>Hi, I'm from Vienna.</i>

283
01:06:19,350 --> 01:06:22,896
<i>What should I say?
It's my first time doing this.</i>

284
01:06:24,564 --> 01:06:26,691
<i>I like to cook, watch movies.</i>

285
01:06:27,275 --> 01:06:30,862
<i>But I also enjoy spending
the evening watching TV.</i>

286
01:06:31,446 --> 01:06:32,739
Look.

287
01:06:45,168 --> 01:06:46,211
Go away!

288
01:06:48,171 --> 01:06:49,464
Help me.

289
01:06:57,013 --> 01:06:58,306
Stop it!

290
01:06:59,682 --> 01:07:00,850
Stop!

291
01:07:01,893 --> 01:07:04,604
I don't see it.
- What are you doing?

292
01:07:04,687 --> 01:07:05,897
Take another look.

293
01:07:06,773 --> 01:07:09,776
What is this? What is this?

294
01:07:10,235 --> 01:07:13,696
In the video your eyes are brown.
- What?

295
01:07:14,781 --> 01:07:18,576
They're contacts, Christ!
They're in the bathroom.

296
01:07:36,928 --> 01:07:38,888
Why are you lying to me?

297
01:07:44,644 --> 01:07:47,564
I thought we agreed not to believe her.

298
01:07:47,814 --> 01:07:50,108
So? I changed my mind.

299
01:07:50,483 --> 01:07:52,777
Do you believe her, you retard?

300
01:07:52,986 --> 01:07:54,445
You're the retard!

301
01:08:19,053 --> 01:08:20,388
<i>Help!</i>

302
01:08:27,228 --> 01:08:29,230
Where are the damn scissors?

303
01:08:30,189 --> 01:08:32,859
Do you understand? Get the scissors!

304
01:08:44,245 --> 01:08:45,496
Lukas?

305
01:08:53,046 --> 01:08:54,130
<i>Elias...</i>

306
01:08:56,132 --> 01:08:57,258
Lukas?

307
01:08:59,719 --> 01:09:02,013
Sit beside me. Come on.

308
01:09:03,014 --> 01:09:05,016
Come, Elias. Sit here.

309
01:09:08,561 --> 01:09:10,605
Come sit beside me, Elias.

310
01:09:14,651 --> 01:09:17,320
Come on, sit down. So we can talk.

311
01:09:19,739 --> 01:09:20,865
Look.

312
01:09:26,663 --> 01:09:27,830
<i>Elias...</i>

313
01:09:29,666 --> 01:09:31,876
You know I'm your mom.

314
01:09:47,850 --> 01:09:49,477
I can't untie myself.

315
01:09:49,727 --> 01:09:55,274
Just go to the bathroom,
get the scissors and cut me loose.

316
01:10:00,071 --> 01:10:02,949
Nothing bad has happened. Cut me loose.

317
01:10:05,785 --> 01:10:09,414
<i>I want you to say 10 times,
"I won't listen to my brother."</i>

318
01:10:09,831 --> 01:10:12,333
<i>I won't listen to my brother.
I won't...</i>

319
01:10:12,583 --> 01:10:13,918
<i>Louder, please.</i>

320
01:10:14,043 --> 01:10:17,296
<i>I won't listen to my brother.
I won't listen...</i>

321
01:10:17,463 --> 01:10:18,923
<i>I said louder.</i>

322
01:10:20,591 --> 01:10:22,719
Our mom wouldn't do that.

323
01:10:22,844 --> 01:10:23,970
<i>More clearly.</i>

324
01:10:24,971 --> 01:10:26,055
<i>Elias...</i>

325
01:10:28,599 --> 01:10:29,934
I'm sorry.

326
01:10:30,268 --> 01:10:31,519
<i>Again.</i>

327
01:10:31,978 --> 01:10:33,771
I'm sorry, Elias.

328
01:10:44,615 --> 01:10:45,908
Come now.

329
01:10:46,909 --> 01:10:48,745
Please. Cut me loose.

330
01:10:56,753 --> 01:10:58,379
What happened to your nose?

331
01:10:59,380 --> 01:11:01,716
Nothing. Nothing serious.

332
01:11:02,550 --> 01:11:04,051
There, you see?

333
01:11:08,139 --> 01:11:09,766
You'll cut me loose

334
01:11:10,308 --> 01:11:12,143
and I'll make you breakfast.

335
01:11:13,019 --> 01:11:15,354
Cut my feet loose, they hurt.

336
01:11:21,277 --> 01:11:22,361
Lukas?

337
01:11:23,863 --> 01:11:26,532
I know it's hard, but we'll make it.

338
01:11:27,200 --> 01:11:29,660
Come, just cut my feet loose.

339
01:11:34,707 --> 01:11:38,002
Come on, it'll take a sec.
I'll make breakfast.

340
01:11:42,673 --> 01:11:43,966
Just cut it.

341
01:11:46,761 --> 01:11:47,929
That's it.

342
01:11:52,225 --> 01:11:53,643
What are you doing?

343
01:12:03,027 --> 01:12:04,070
There.

344
01:12:06,364 --> 01:12:07,365
What?

345
01:12:12,203 --> 01:12:14,205
What is it?

346
01:12:17,708 --> 01:12:18,709
<i>5&0? -</i>

347
01:12:21,295 --> 01:12:23,714
They had to remove it in hospital.

348
01:12:24,715 --> 01:12:26,342
They're dangerous.

349
01:12:27,176 --> 01:12:28,511
Liar!

350
01:12:30,304 --> 01:12:31,722
They had to. They had no...

351
01:12:32,265 --> 01:12:34,684
Admit that it's a lie.

352
01:12:36,602 --> 01:12:38,896
Just cut me loose, please.

353
01:12:49,407 --> 01:12:50,449
<i>Stop.</i>

354
01:12:51,033 --> 01:12:52,076
<i>Stop!</i>

355
01:13:18,811 --> 01:13:20,813
Tell us where our mom is.

356
01:13:26,986 --> 01:13:29,071
Tell us where our mom is!

357
01:15:33,863 --> 01:15:35,072
It's open.

358
01:15:35,906 --> 01:15:38,200
Hello, Red Cross!

359
01:15:40,953 --> 01:15:41,996
Hello?

360
01:15:43,164 --> 01:15:45,750
Red Cross. Care to make a donation?

361
01:15:46,208 --> 01:15:47,752
Is anybody home?

362
01:15:51,380 --> 01:15:52,882
I'll have a look.

363
01:15:56,427 --> 01:15:57,553
Hello?

364
01:15:58,012 --> 01:15:59,221
Red Cross.

365
01:16:03,059 --> 01:16:04,351
Nobody's there.

366
01:16:08,314 --> 01:16:11,442
It was unlocked, someone must be home.

367
01:16:17,656 --> 01:16:18,824
Hello?

368
01:16:21,744 --> 01:16:23,204
Maybe they're upstairs.

369
01:16:30,086 --> 01:16:31,504
Red Cross.

370
01:16:34,799 --> 01:16:36,550
Hello?
- Hello!

371
01:16:37,051 --> 01:16:38,135
Hello.

372
01:16:43,641 --> 01:16:44,975
Is your mom home?

373
01:16:46,018 --> 01:16:47,520
No, she's not home.

374
01:16:47,728 --> 01:16:50,022
Not upstairs? We heard something.

375
01:16:50,272 --> 01:16:52,191
No, that's our dog.

376
01:16:52,525 --> 01:16:54,193
She's not home?
- No.

377
01:16:54,485 --> 01:16:55,653
It's our dog.

378
01:16:57,696 --> 01:16:59,907
When will Mom be back?

379
01:17:05,996 --> 01:17:07,665
She'll be home soon.

380
01:17:09,083 --> 01:17:10,334
Can we wait?

381
01:17:10,960 --> 01:17:12,336
Where should we wait?

382
01:17:23,389 --> 01:17:27,351
Hand me the list.
I'll see how much we've collected.

383
01:17:27,476 --> 01:17:30,479
The money too?
- Yeah, I'll count it.

384
01:17:31,147 --> 01:17:33,774
Really bad handwriting.
- Yeah.

385
01:17:33,983 --> 01:17:37,027
You'd swear a doctor had written it.

386
01:17:37,153 --> 01:17:39,029
It's barely legible.

387
01:17:40,781 --> 01:17:42,950
Looking forward to school?

388
01:17:43,367 --> 01:17:45,369
Well...
- It starts soon.

389
01:17:50,166 --> 01:17:53,586
Where did you go to school before?
- In Vienna.

390
01:17:56,005 --> 01:17:58,382
A lot more going on there.

391
01:18:03,929 --> 01:18:06,682
We've already collected a tidy sum.

392
01:18:06,807 --> 01:18:09,810
If somebody else gives as much as him,

393
01:18:10,060 --> 01:18:12,688
we'll have done pretty well.

394
01:18:15,065 --> 01:18:17,985
We'll see how much more we get.

395
01:18:18,402 --> 01:18:20,821
What do you do all day?

396
01:18:21,113 --> 01:18:22,573
Not much.

397
01:18:33,000 --> 01:18:34,960
I have to go to the toilet.

398
01:19:05,741 --> 01:19:07,284
Is your mom back?

399
01:19:07,534 --> 01:19:08,786
Not yet.

400
01:19:09,119 --> 01:19:12,206
Is that your own money?

401
01:19:12,414 --> 01:19:13,540
No.

402
01:19:16,919 --> 01:19:21,465
Will your mom be OK with this?
- Yes, I'm sure she will.

403
01:19:22,633 --> 01:19:24,718
She always gives that much.

404
01:19:26,887 --> 01:19:29,223
We don't want any trouble.

405
01:19:29,306 --> 01:19:30,975
You realize that...

406
01:19:32,393 --> 01:19:36,105
We usually don't
accept money from children.

407
01:19:36,230 --> 01:19:38,148
That's a lot of money.

408
01:19:38,274 --> 01:19:40,150
No, we're allowed.

409
01:19:40,985 --> 01:19:43,570
Well, it is a nice house. Just look.

410
01:19:43,696 --> 01:19:46,323
I guess they can afford it.

411
01:19:52,329 --> 01:19:54,665
As a thank-you for the donation,

412
01:19:55,291 --> 01:19:56,750
here's a Band-Aid.

413
01:20:02,172 --> 01:20:03,340
Help!

414
01:20:04,842 --> 01:20:07,845
<i>Help! Help!</i>

415
01:20:08,012 --> 01:20:10,973
Help! Help!

416
01:20:33,287 --> 01:20:35,247
Stop! Stop!

417
01:23:41,391 --> 01:23:44,561
Please prove you're our mom.

418
01:23:54,988 --> 01:23:58,033
Ask her what my favorite song is.

419
01:23:59,243 --> 01:24:01,453
What's Lukas' favorite song?

420
01:24:11,588 --> 01:24:13,507
Lullaby and Good Night?

421
01:24:46,748 --> 01:24:47,874
Don't!

422
01:25:04,308 --> 01:25:08,812
<i>Can you count the stars that brightly</i>

423
01:25:09,313 --> 01:25:13,066
<i>Twinkle in the midnight sky?</i>

424
01:25:14,026 --> 01:25:18,196
<i>Can you count the clouds, so lightly</i>

425
01:25:18,822 --> 01:25:22,701
<i>O'er the meadows floating by?</i>

426
01:25:23,452 --> 01:25:27,789
<i>God, the Lord, doth mark their number</i>

427
01:25:28,123 --> 01:25:32,085
<i>With His eyes that never slumber</i>

428
01:25:32,586 --> 01:25:36,214
<i>You He sees and you He loves</i>

429
01:25:36,715 --> 01:25:39,968
<i>You He sees and you He loves</i>

430
01:26:01,865 --> 01:26:03,909
Where's our mom?

431
01:27:07,597 --> 01:27:09,766
Don't you know when you
have to pee?

432
01:27:11,643 --> 01:27:13,687
We're not changing them.

433
01:27:15,480 --> 01:27:16,565
Hello?

434
01:27:21,194 --> 01:27:22,571
Untie me.

435
01:28:21,213 --> 01:28:22,923
Now change the bed.

436
01:28:23,340 --> 01:28:24,966
Take off the sheets.

437
01:28:27,636 --> 01:28:29,846
Come on, take them off.

438
01:30:36,389 --> 01:30:37,515
Elias?

439
01:30:38,600 --> 01:30:40,185
Where's our mom?

440
01:30:42,020 --> 01:30:43,605
Elias, come here.

441
01:30:45,065 --> 01:30:46,691
Where is she?

442
01:30:53,239 --> 01:30:54,324
Fine.

443
01:30:56,368 --> 01:30:58,703
Elias, let's make a deal.

444
01:31:00,121 --> 01:31:01,790
I'll play along again.

445
01:31:03,333 --> 01:31:05,502
I'll talk to Lukas again.

446
01:31:06,920 --> 01:31:08,713
Lukas will be alive.

447
01:31:14,094 --> 01:31:16,179
I'll make you both breakfast,

448
01:31:16,429 --> 01:31:20,058
put out your clothes.
We'll do things, like before.

449
01:31:20,183 --> 01:31:22,352
But you have to believe me

450
01:31:22,936 --> 01:31:24,688
that I'm your mom.

451
01:31:27,983 --> 01:31:30,151
You won't really do that.

452
01:31:35,448 --> 01:31:36,866
I promise.

453
01:31:38,827 --> 01:31:39,953
<i>Elias...</i>

454
01:31:41,871 --> 01:31:44,749
It's not your fault Lukas died.

455
01:31:46,793 --> 01:31:49,546
The accident wasn't your fault.

456
01:31:51,464 --> 01:31:53,717
Do you really believe her?

457
01:32:02,392 --> 01:32:03,435
She's lying.

458
01:32:09,816 --> 01:32:12,527
Let her prove she's our mom.

459
01:32:19,117 --> 01:32:20,744
What am I doing?

460
01:32:21,870 --> 01:32:23,788
What's Lukas doing?

461
01:32:29,002 --> 01:32:31,087
But I can't see him!

462
01:32:31,421 --> 01:32:33,298
What's he doing?

463
01:32:39,262 --> 01:32:40,597
<i>Elias...</i>

464
01:32:44,142 --> 01:32:46,227
Mom would know that.

465
01:32:47,771 --> 01:32:49,606
Mom could see him.

466
01:32:51,900 --> 01:32:54,110
She'd know what he's doing.

467
01:33:04,120 --> 01:33:05,622
No, Elias. Don't!

468
01:33:07,749 --> 01:33:09,125
Elias, don't!

469
01:33:09,793 --> 01:33:11,503
Elias, do you hear me?

470
01:33:25,100 --> 01:33:27,185
Help! Help!

471
01:35:29,432 --> 01:35:33,436
<i>God, the Lord, doth mark their number</i>

472
01:35:33,519 --> 01:35:37,815
<i>With His eyes that never slumber</i>

473
01:35:37,899 --> 01:35:41,778
<i>You He sees and you He loves</i>

474
01:35:41,861 --> 01:35:46,282
<i>You He sees and you He loves</i>

